                                                        <p class="brfprofile">
                                                            A PhD in management on “Entrepreneurial Success” from Amity
                                                            University, Noida, Prof.(Dr.) Shalini Sharma is currently
                                                            working as Associate Professor and holding the
                                                            responsibility of Dean-Outreach and Student Welfare at GIMS,
                                                            Greater Noida. Her research interests include
                                                            Entrepreneurial psychology, algorithmic management and
                                                            control, neurodiversity and skill development. She has quite
                                                            a few Scopus , ABDC and ABS indexed publications. She is NLP
                                                            (Practitioner) and TTT certified from the British Council,
                                                            New Delhi. Has a diversified work experience of academics,
                                                            sales and HR & administration .
                                                            <br>
                                                            <br>
                                                            Her passion for training has got her association with V V
                                                            Giri National Labour Institute, Noida where she imparts
                                                            trainings in behavioural areas to various PSU personnel
                                                            including the police officers and RBI personnel on regular
                                                            basis and the trade union leaders from across the country.
                                                            She has developed and delivered several training modules for
                                                            the government personnel and many private houses. She has
                                                            been actively involved in various research, consulting and
                                                            training assignments with V V Giri National Labur Institute,
                                                            MDI, Gurgaon, B. M.L. Munjal University, Manesar, ISAB, New
                                                            Delhi, Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA). She
                                                            has designed and delivered MDP and SDP and corporate
                                                            training sessions for the ex-servicemen (JSOs), Police
                                                            Personnel, Personnel from The Reserve Bank of India,
                                                            Ministry of Women and Child Empowerment ICAR- Coimbatore,
                                                            Lennox International, leaders of various Trade Unions,
                                                            Eninov Systems, IIFM, Quantico Education and Management
                                                            Services to name a few. She had been instrumental in
                                                            organizing the National Seminar on “Make in India for
                                                            Defense Forces” for the Western Command, Indian Army.
                                                        </p>
